{#
/**
 * @file
 * split-masthead — the two-column masthead (src/components/page-header.css,
 * `.page-header--split`): the news article's head (templates/news-article.html)
 * worn by any Canvas page. The heading sits left in the article headline's
 * serif, with a slot above and a slot below it — the article puts its back
 * link and its category / date row there — and the right column is a slot
 * for whatever the page wants beside it. The heading speaks one of three
 * voices (--serif, --caps, --sentence) with an optional eyebrow over it in
 * the Masthead's accent voice (user ask, Sep 2026: "select any of the H1s
 * styles we have … the eyebrow text (can that be an option above)") (user ask, Sep 2026: "like the two
 * column news, but with our H1 header on the left and optional block above
 * and below. Block on right to add whatever").
 *
 * The opening (which <html> class hands over as the masthead scrolls away)
 * is the Masthead's: the class is put on <html> by icon_preprocess_html()
 * reading this component off the page; here the masthead only names it for
 * js/theme-handover.js. dark-hold is not mapped on purpose: it opens dark
 * and never hands over.
 */
#}
{% set tag = heading_level|default('h1') %}
{% set style = style|default('caps') %} {# caps by default (user call, 23 Sep 2026: a new split masthead should open on the eyebrow and the caps H1, not the article serif) #}
{% set handover_class = attribute({ dark: 'dark', blue: 'theme-blue', 'light-grey': 'theme-work-article', custom: 'theme-work-article' }, opening|default('none'))|default('') %}
<div class="page-header page-header--split"{% if handover_class %} data-theme-handover data-theme-handover-class="{{ handover_class }}"{% endif %}>
  <div class="page-header__split">
    {# the column's own hairlines, top and bottom (user call, 23 Sep 2026:
       "update the split masthead to have line top and bottom") — drawn in
       like every rule (utilities/rules.css); the above and below slots sit
       inside them #}
    <div class="page-header__split-intro" data-rule="both">
      <div class="page-header__split-above">{% block above %}{{ above }}{% endblock %}</div>
      {# the shared word cascade (data-reveal-words, js/reveal.js) — the About
         lockup's and the work masthead's entrance, on this title too (user
         call, 23 Sep 2026: "can all mastheads have it for consistency?");
         the eyebrow's word leads, the title's follow #}
      <{{ tag }} class="page-header__split-title page-header__split-title--{{ style }}" data-reveal-words>
        {%- if eyebrow -%}<span class="page-header__split-eyebrow masthead-accent">{{ eyebrow }}</span>{%- endif -%}
        <span class="page-header__split-text">{{ title|nl2br }}</span>
      </{{ tag }}>
      <div class="page-header__split-below">{% block below %}{{ below }}{% endblock %}</div>
    </div>
    <div class="page-header__split-aside">{% block aside %}{{ aside }}{% endblock %}</div>
  </div>
</div>
